    {
      "id": "p00002",
      "text": "\"Eat, drink, sleep,\" said she, \"and may our lady of Atocha,[9] the great\nSt. Anthony of Padua, and the great St. James of Compostella, receive\nyou under their protection.",
      "translation": "Mangez, buvez, dormez, lui\ndit-elle, et que Notre-Dame d’Atocha[1], monseigneur saint Antoine de\nPadoue, et monseigneur saint Jacques de Compostelle prennent soin de\nvous!",
      "paragraph_id": "en-p00002",
      "target_paragraph_id": "fr-p00001",
      "languages": {
        "base": "en",
        "learning": "fr"
      },
      "replacements": [],
      "sentences": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p00003",
      "text": "I shall be back to-morrow.\"",
      "translation": "je reviendrai demain.",
      "paragraph_id": "en-p00002",
      "target_paragraph_id": "fr-p00001",
      "languages": {
        "base": "en",
        "learning": "fr"
      },
      "replacements": [],
      "sentences": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p00004",
      "text": "Candide, amazed at all he had suffered and still more with the charity\nof the old woman, wished to kiss her hand.",
      "translation": "Candide, toujours étonné de tout ce qu’il\navait vu, de tout ce qu’il avait souffert, et encore plus de la charité\nde la vieille, voulut lui baiser la main.",
      "paragraph_id": "en-p00003",
      "target_paragraph_id": "fr-p00001",
      "languages": {
        "base": "en",
        "learning": "fr"
      },
